{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview","id":1509727,"title":"Glass Walkers have won the poll for a preview.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-26T08:49:12-07:00","id":1509727,"title":"Glass Walkers have won the poll for a preview.","content":"There's a preview of them at Renegade page for werewofl","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T09:52:57-07:00","id":1509739,"title":"","content":"<img width=\"1280\" height=\"819\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/7GPromc.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/7GPromc.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/7GPromc.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Here is the full image without the silly viewer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T11:29:19-07:00","id":1509753,"title":"","content":"Why did the Tribe least likely to change notably in W5 win the poll? Did people not want to know stuff? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T11:30:06-07:00","id":1509754,"title":"","content":"That not breaking things Ban throws all those Glass Walker Monkey Wrenchers into a bit of a bind....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T12:27:55-07:00","id":1509761,"title":"","content":"I guess the Jam Technology gift circumvents the ban because it doesn't actually damage the item, just renders it inert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T16:15:40-07:00","id":1509794,"title":"","content":"It's a bit hard to judge too much without seeing what the other Tribes are getting (they could all have equally niche bonuses and hefty bans).<br /> <br /> My big take aware from reading this is that I was right to be worried that the decoupling of Tribe and human culture would result in there not being enough narrative space for 11 Tribes. This take on the Glass Walkers has them taking bits from the Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia's past roles in the story. Removing the Wise Guy and Corporate Wolves side of the Glass Walkers where they approach cities from a top-down perspective (hence the idea of them walking among the glass of skyscrapers), makes them way more overlapping with the bottom-up approach of the Bone Gnawers (who previously had the &quot;Robin Hood&quot; niche as their thing), and the community organizer parts of the Children of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T17:13:40-07:00","id":1509801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509794#post1509794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bit hard to judge too much without seeing what the other Tribes are getting (they could all have equally niche bonuses and hefty bans).<br /> <br /> My big take aware from reading this is that I was right to be worried that the decoupling of Tribe and human culture would result in there not being enough narrative space for 11 Tribes. This take on the Glass Walkers has them taking bits from the Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia's past roles in the story. Removing the Wise Guy and Corporate Wolves side of the Glass Walkers where they approach cities from a top-down perspective (hence the idea of them walking among the glass of skyscrapers), makes them way more overlapping with the bottom-up approach of the Bone Gnawers (who previously had the &quot;Robin Hood&quot; niche as their thing), and the community organizer parts of the Children of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure you can still play those camps archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T17:35:49-07:00","id":1509804,"title":"","content":"&quot;Can play&quot; is &quot;W5 will support you playing,&quot; are different things. It seems very likely the Silver Fangs or Shadow Lords are going to end up much better for people that want to play werewolves ruling human organization style characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T17:39:18-07:00","id":1509805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509801#post1509801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure you can still play those camps archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about the ability to play them, and more about giving clear direction for players.<br /> <br /> Games often run a risk of creating choice paralysis in a desire to cover as much playstyle and character interest as possible, which can be a problem for anyone who comes in not knowing exactly what they want to do (which even for veterans in a game is going to be a problem that can and will happen between editions). This is a very particular problem for World of Darkness games that tends to build lots and lots of major avenues for determing your character.<br /> <br /> One of the important things for dealing with that problem is having clear delineation, removing as much overlap as possible. You want to write your character options in such a way where that if someone says &quot;I want to play something like X, but with a bit of Y&quot; you can rapidly point them to what has X and what has Y, hopefully in a way that doesn't require a whole lot of retrofitting. Being able to go &quot;Community Organizers are Children of Gaia, Robin Hoods are Bone Gnawers, Corporate Wolves are Glass Walkers&quot; allows for people to sharply get an idea or get to their idea quicker and more efficiently, get into play faster, and more quickly figure out what their character would do in gameplay.<br /> <br /> It's also good for just flavor purposes-the more hats a particular option can wear, the more muddled and indistinct they become, particularly as giving breadth takes away from the particulars of how and for what reasoning any given option does a particular thing. The Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers, on this particular direction, already kind of a shared problem in being regarded, from the outside, as being the urban/homid Tribes who are only different because of their economic class. The more the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers can wear each other's distinctives hats, the less important it is that they're different, and can even grossly over appeal to the Glass Walker <i>because</i> of the class distinction.<br /> <br /> There's a general idea among serious content creators that it's better to do one thing really well and dynamically then make an attempt to do everything to a mediocre level. The increased homogeneity of the Glass Walkers in this preview, as an indicator, indicates that reading up on the Tribes is going to be more boring and encourage less vivid flights of character creation. Players, of course, can and already will bend a system to accomodate a vision they come in with, but for everyone else, this is less likely to draw in and inspire than it should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:08:28-07:00","id":1509806,"title":"","content":"I think the limiting factor in terms of the presentation here is that the only thing this write-up is really interested in is simply &quot;Tribe is <i>what </i>you do.&quot; and more specifically &quot;This Tribe is <i>these four verbs</i> that you do.&quot;. And it wants to avoid the reader thinking too much about this beyond that. Like it wants to avoid &quot;Who are the Glass Walker?&quot; turning into Lore (ie facts and/or ideas anyone should memorize to understand the Tribe) as much as possible. Through that lens, the difference will be that Bone Gnawers will give you four different verbs with a different Favor and Ban.<br /> <br /> Will it be consistent and balanced? Who knows... But H5 didn't manage to do it with five Creed-fields in explaining when what Creed can use Desperation-Dice to boost their dice-pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:16:50-07:00","id":1509808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509806#post1509806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the limiting factor in terms of the presentation here is that the only thing this write-up is really interested in is simply &quot;Tribe is <i>what </i>you do.&quot; and more specifically &quot;This Tribe is <i>these four verbs</i> that you do.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;That's too many [verbs], put them back.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:38:20-07:00","id":1509813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509808#post1509808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;That's too many [verbs], put them back.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If it goes down the <i>exact same</i> road as H5, the moment you look at the system you'll realize that really the only thing that mattered on those two pages is the Favor and Ban. Everything else you can discard. During the game you'll just start to look at werewolves as this indistinguishable mass with various Favors/Ban-pairs that turn into a hierarchy of which ones are fun to play and which ones aren't. Because the Tribes are just that irrelevant to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:43:32-07:00","id":1509814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509813#post1509813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it goes down the <i>exact same</i> road as H5, the moment you look at the system you'll realize that really the only thing that mattered on those two pages is the Favor and Ban. Everything else you can discard. During the game you'll just start to look at werewolves as this indistinguishable mass with various Favors/Ban-pairs that turn into a hierarchy of which ones are fun to play and which ones aren't. Because the Tribes are just that irrelevant to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just remembering how there was a pushback on how Chronicles took a more archetypal approach to it's character types than the more specific inclination of World on the whole and wondering if anyone at Paradox was there for that fight. It seems like it would have been a good learning moment for them.<br /> <br /> (and keep in mind, I say that as someone who favors how Chronicles handled being more archetypal)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T19:55:56-07:00","id":1509823,"title":"","content":"Hey folkx. A similar discussion happened earlier in the official wod discord. Justin Achilli showed up.<br /> his comments seem to indicate that we shouldn't worry too much about tribes being irrelevant,there is indeed tribe flavour. Your choice of tribe does affect your character. At least from the comments old and new that I've found","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T20:23:44-07:00","id":1509828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509823#post1509823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey folkx. A similar discussion happened earlier in the official wod discord. Justin Achilli showed up.<br /> his comments seem to indicate that we shouldn't worry too much about tribes being irrelevant,there is indeed tribe flavour. Your choice of tribe does affect your character. At least from the comments old and new that I've found</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's nice and all, but you know what would be even better? If the sample text provided in a preview communicated that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T20:34:05-07:00","id":1509830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509828#post1509828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's nice and all, but you know what would be even better? If the sample text provided in a preview communicated that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be wrong. But I'm pretty sure that tribe identity is communicated also through your Tribe deciding which Gifts we have,which spirit items we'll get access to and which spirits we deal with and the like.<br /> But also,since those analysis are all very subjective, I'll say the Glass Walkers in this two page spread did have an strong identity to me.<br /> the archetypes are all examples of Werewolves who deal with people,and how they manipulate systems including but not limited to machines to their own ends.<br /> I obviously haven't seem the Children of Gaia spreadsheet but I can't imagine it will the same focus on dealing with people as systems and manipulating systems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T22:41:20-07:00","id":1509837,"title":"","content":"I find the writeup concise but informative, in the line of V5 Clan writeups: it tells you what Glass Walkers do, their relation with Garou Society at large, and gives you some concrete ideas how to play it.<br /> <br /> It also quite clearly states that Walkers are distrusted because other Wolves think they supported Humies during the Impergium.<br /> <br /> The fact is that the expectations of many are set towards another concept of Glass Walkers, I think, and another format of presentation.<br /> <br /> Presentation issue first. <br /> <br /> If we go back to V3 or V2 or V1 Clan writeups (I do not own other Werewolf corebooks besides W20, but I suppose the tone would be similar) , they weren't frontloaded with much setting info. That, was reserved for general fluff chapter and later supplements.<br /> <br /> V20 changed that format, due to the unique conditions of its birth: problem is, as we saw that kind of format was good for agnostic omnibus editions but difficult to maintain when you had a whole editorial line to support.<br /> <br /> What would you write in later supplements? If we look at many X20 supplements, they are either more omnibus formats (Lore of the X, Rites of Blood etc.) or far smaller books. <br /> <br /> At one point, they had to think of another edition to go on with publishing that kind of content, the space for agnostic stand alone supplements had ran out. <br /> <br /> Also, those kind of books were aimed at an expert fanbase: we long time fans CRAVE lots of information densely packed in one place.<br /> <br /> BJD and Apocalyptic Records are like Sunday happening on Monday with Ice Cream pouring from the Sky.<br /> <br /> When you are creating a new edition of a game, aimed at newbies, frontloading the splat page with setting details is risky, in terms of accessibility.<br /> <br /> Second point, we are looking at these Glass Walkers thinking of Legacy Glass Walkers.<br /> <br /> Taking into account this is a reboot, everything from imagery to archetypes to practical declination of verbs says that the &quot;new&quot; Glass Walkers are not Cyberpunk Corpos, but NeoNoir Hackers and Social Planners. They are close to Humanity, fixated with tech and want to navigate society and its many facets.<br /> <br /> A mix of Nosferatu and Toreadors, possibly, to stick with Vampire references. Some of their space surely is overlapping with OLD Gnawers and COGs but the important thing to look at is what the NEW tribes will be up to, confronted with the NEW Walkers.<br /> <br /> For instance, what few things we have learned about the COGs seems to make them much less diplomats and social activitsts, and much more priests and lorekeepers. As for Gnawers, if they and the Walkers are not distinguished by class, I'm curious to see where the difference will be.<br /> <br /> I actually like what I see, but I'm probably more in target of W5 than most of the forumites: I never went into old Werewolf because it had a very distinct terminology and complex metaplot.<br /> <br /> Which probably was part of its appeal and beauty, as I'm very fond of Vampire's own byzantine jargon and metaplot.<br /> <br /> However, we legacy players have the X20 editions to use for our philological needs: when they are trying to make a version of the game &quot;as written in these times&quot;, aiming to a, new fanbase, I fully expect enough familiarity for old time players to jump on ship, but enough changes to justify the adaptation and a presentation of the materials which is simple enough to immediately grasp it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 04-27-2023, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T23:26:23-07:00","id":1509840,"title":"","content":"Ultimately though, they chose to make this the WoD 5th Edition, not the new new World of Darkness. This is Werewolf: the Apocalypse, not Werewolf: the Extinction. These are the Glass Walkers, not the Humanists.<br /> <br /> If they want to make a game where people aren't going to look at how the old and new look next to each other, they should have made something far more distinct. Plenty of people involved with V5 and W5 saw how much people did this to the cWoD vs. nWoD which were explicitly different universes with different settings and different takes on similar concepts. Of course it's going to be worse when they're keeping the original 13 Tribes, and then heavily redefining them (something V5 largely did not do).<br /> <br /> If they want to claim they're honoring the spirit of WtA 1e? This isn't it. If they're trying to make this easier to digest for new players? There's plenty of jargon that makes no sense unless you've internalized the lexicon.<br /> <br /> Like I said, the big problem with just this small snippet, is that 11 Tribes feel like too many for what they're doing and they needed to keep 11 Tribes because they want to keep the legacy of WtA attached. Maybe I'm wrong and after some more previews we'll see that 11 didn't overload the game's new direction, but this isn't a good start to convincing me otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T23:47:09-07:00","id":1509841,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12590\" data-vbnamecard=\"12590\">Manfr</a> At least for me, it isn't really as much that the preview does not match OG GWs, because I expected it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> What bothers me is the lack of 'werewolf' in the writing, All of the example characters could be played as human or Kin PCs with virtually no changes. If the point of the game is that garou don't have it easy dealing with humanity, this preview does not match it.<br /> <br /> Second, the preview still uses the 'GW have almost no lupus and they feel they are losing the wolf' from OG GWs. But W5 is a reboot and as such it doesn't have the baggage with lupus that W20 had. As such, the potential pool of wolves would be much bigger. Such as wolfdogs, coywolves, dingos, and even pariah dogs. There are urban canines to choose from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T00:16:40-07:00","id":1509843,"title":"","content":"I think what you are both saying is absolutely logical and understandable. <br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, WOD5 has apparently pivoted away from the &quot;bring back 1st edition&quot; of Team Ericsson and embraced the idea of rebooting the game entirely, bringing parts of the old WOD and COFD together in the process not just in terms of mechanics but also of tone and presentation. <br /> <br /> It's going into unsafe waters, and naturally invites comparison: perhaps it will pay off nonetheless, as it will allow them to draw on familiar brands but with greater creative freedom. Let's hope we do not end up in Star Wars Sequel territory. <br /> <br /> Regarding the writeups, I agree we shall have to see if they can manage them without falling into redundancy: I'm a bit more optimistic after this one, as they are reworking concepts from the scratch, basically. <br /> <br /> That said, the writeup is quite simple, it draws on two-three lore concepts presented before, but it stays into the right thematic territory, IMHO. Wolf is not particularly there, but urban animism and a certain urban fantasy theme are there. If anything, it is a bit mageish. <br /> <br /> As for urban dogs, very true, I wonder if we will see something about them with the Gnawers. Contrast with Walkers might also be that Gnawers have accepted to &quot;dilute their wolfishness&quot; to adapt? Perhaps they will be more crime-connected or community-oriented, reflecting their embrace of domesticated canines? I'm curious. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T00:48:27-07:00","id":1509844,"title":"","content":"With &quot;losing the wolf&quot;, I just remembered that the same phrase came up during the Discord Q&amp;A:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Can you elaborate on how the shapeshifting mechanics will work? Will forms and shifting be tied to Rage, perhaps into a Rage Dice mechanic?</b><br /> Still in development, but emphasizes Rage being a double-edged sword. You don't want to be overwhelmed by Rage, but you don't want to &quot;lose the wolf&quot; in a critical moment. </div> </div> </div>So the same way the Hauglosk we heard about in relation to the Get seems to be something every Garou can experience (as it's tied to Rage), I guess &quot;losing the wolf&quot; is also something that every Garou can potentially experience.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T00:52:45-07:00","id":1509845,"title":"","content":"Outstar, like a week ago, was talking about how W5 is a mix of going back to the 1e WtA roots and rebooting to make it fit for &quot;modern times.&quot; Which isn't really any different from what Ericsson said when he was doing press for V5. So no, that idea hasn't been dropped. They're still trying to sell W5 as both something for old school fans and fans in the making.<br /> <br /> The problem for WtA specifically, is that WtA was probably the least changed WoD game that got editions for every iteration of the WoD. The W20 presentation of the Tribes really isn't that different from the 1e. If the W5 Tribes depart too much from their core identifies, then the book's failed on something promised as the previews have started coming out more regularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T01:23:11-07:00","id":1509933,"title":"","content":"That's why I hoped for Red Talons, cause Glass Walkers core is usually the same and I expected something like I saw in preview.<br /> Talons are anti human tribe, and I have suspicion that W5 will change this tribe most. That would give me and idea how W5 might look.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T03:18:54-07:00","id":1509939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509933#post1509933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I hoped for Red Talons, cause Glass Walkers core is usually the same and I expected something like I saw in preview.<br /> Talons are anti human tribe, and I have suspicion that W5 will change this tribe most. That would give me and idea how W5 might look.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how much worse would it be, if the Talons hadn't changed at all aside from now allowing humans within their ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T06:56:28-07:00","id":1509952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509939#post1509939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And how much worse would it be, if the Talons hadn't changed at all aside from now allowing humans within their ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of like the Bender-ification of the Red Talons. &quot;Hey sexy mama, wanna kill all humans?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T08:20:30-07:00","id":1509958,"title":"","content":"I would not understand that kind of change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T09:27:38-07:00","id":1509962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509939#post1509939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how much worse would it be, if the Talons hadn't changed at all aside from now allowing humans within their ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the whole switch to the Garou-Kin-dynamic just amounts to the book saying &quot;It's not the bad, old WtA! It's new!&quot; but the effort put into it just amounts to &quot;It's not hereditary anymore, I swear!&quot; and the Tribe-descriptions are still superficially recapitulating the same narrative beats as in previous editions, then that would be very disappointing and more specifically what was the point of making it a reboot in the first place then? The whole thing would just feel like a cheap cop-out. It would mean the Garou-Kin-dynamic was introduced to simply say &quot;It's not hereditary! Purebreed, Kinfolk etc... All that bad stuff is gone!&quot; but there's no new paradigm and/or worldbuilding to replace it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T10:29:30-07:00","id":1509968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509939#post1509939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And how much worse would it be, if the Talons hadn't changed at all aside from now allowing humans within their ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember where a read, I guess it was in the red talons tribebook, the day the red talons accepted a human in their ranks, is the day the tribe will end for good because the Red talons essence is be a wolf tribe, no a Human-Wolf tribe, it's like a Glass Walker living without tecnology, a Fenris without his battlewish fury, a Silent Strider without his wish to travel, a Nosferatu without scars, A Malkavian without insanity and a Redcap without his teeth. I traveled a little too far on this analogy, but you get the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T10:37:05-07:00","id":1509969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509968#post1509968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't remember where a read, I guess it was in the red talons tribebook, the day the red talons accepted a human in their ranks, is the day the tribe will end for good because the Red talons essence is be a wolf tribe, no a Human-Wolf tribe, it's like a Glass Walker living without tecnology, a Fenris without his battlewish fury, a Silent Strider without his wish to travel, a Nosferatu without scars, A Malkavian without insanity and a Redcap without his teeth. I traveled a little too far on this analogy, but you get the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but the philosophy of W5 is that there are no longer tribal restrictions. As such, Red Talons now have homids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T11:27:56-07:00","id":1509971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509968#post1509968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't remember where a read, I guess it was in the red talons tribebook, the day the red talons accepted a human in their ranks, is the day the tribe will end for good because the Red talons essence is be a wolf tribe, no a Human-Wolf tribe, it's like a Glass Walker living without tecnology, a Fenris without his battlewish fury, a Silent Strider without his wish to travel, a Nosferatu without scars, A Malkavian without insanity and a Redcap without his teeth. I traveled a little too far on this analogy, but you get the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before, the idea of these examples was to provide &quot;exceptions to the rule&quot;, to say &quot;You don't <i>have to</i> play this Tribe, Clan, Kith etc. in this one way.&quot; or simply provide some variation in terms of who gets to be a member of these groups. The example from the previews last October was the Black Furies who aren't an all-female-Tribe anymore (and the &quot;all-female&quot; also got its exceptions in the old editions) but the W5-change changed it into a Tribe of Garou who care about injustice. All the restrictions are gone, though. As long as you want to play a Garou who wants to fight injustice (as defined by your player-character), you get to be a Black Fury. Nothing else beyond that matters. And of course, there aren't any connections to Greece and the Mediterranean area anymore (even though their Patron-Spirit is Gorgon now but... I guess &quot;Gorgon&quot; doesn't count as a cultural tie or something).<br /> <br /> And the Red Talons are in the same boat as the Black Furies in that regard.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T13:16:21-07:00","id":1509985,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I wanna see what they do with the Fianna. Fey touched battle poets reveling in life is a strong concept. Not one I expect but pretty damn solid.<br /> <br /> Great Wendigo, Silver Fangs, Uktena, Red Talons and Fianna will probably be the most telling of how much effort they have put into the new tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T13:30:13-07:00","id":1509986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1509969#post1509969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, but the philosophy of W5 is that there are no longer tribal restrictions. As such, Red Talons now have homids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tells me that at least there's something about how they can be homids but have to live like wolves, you know their way, a more primal footprint so to speak, but they could be a bridge to other tribes for knowing what it's like be human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","user":"Psicose","date":". 04-28-2023, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T14:00:40-07:00","id":1509991,"title":"","content":