te\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510146#post1510146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> Them not taking accountability, not apologizing and not offering to make things right. Hell of a statement. Pity they're not telling the community the same thing you said they told you....</div> </div> </div> </div>they are investigating things first. to be sure to not make any more mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-29-2023, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T19:50:44-07:00","id":1510149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510143#post1510143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure thing<br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/status/1652255583070765058?cxt=HHwWhIC2sdzs_u0tAAAA\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/...C2sdzs_u0tAAAA</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I saw that. The thing is... this is just them saying they're aware of the issue and telling people to wait for the real statement on the issue. They haven't addressed it yet. And the longer it takes them to actually address the issue and put out an official statement with an apology and how they want to resolve this situation, the more worrying this whole thing becomes. Because if it were just that one drawing that needed to be dealt with here, this could've been resolved fairly easily, right? So the longer it takes for them to address and resolve this issue, the likelier it is the problem is much bigger than this one drawing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T21:22:59-07:00","id":1510154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510147#post1510147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> they are investigating things first. to be sure to not make any more mistakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by investigating you mean trying to figure out if they can put all the blame on the artist then I would say your statement seems to factually accurate given their reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T21:31:58-07:00","id":1510156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510154#post1510154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If by investigating you mean trying to figure out if they can put all the blame on the artist then I would say your statement seems to factually accurate given their reply.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are trying to make sure the artist didn't do anything wrong on purpose. why exactly do you have such a low opinion of them? they are all good people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T21:35:12-07:00","id":1510157,"title":"","content":"we all must keep in mind,that the rule of of not showing ta moko on art is not common knowledge. it's not somehting taught on the american schools,or european schools. It's not soemthing you know automatically. You have to be told about it to be aware of that rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-30-2023, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T22:29:25-07:00","id":1510162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510157#post1510157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we all must keep in mind,that the rule of of not showing ta moko on art is not common knowledge. it's not somehting taught on the american schools,or european schools. It's not soemthing you know automatically. You have to be told about it to be aware of that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean people have a responsibility to look into the culture they choose to incorporate into their works? What do you think this is 2023? <br /> <br /> You know what is taught in America. Schools? Don't plagiarize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T22:43:55-07:00","id":1510163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510156#post1510156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are trying to make sure the artist didn't do anything wrong on purpose. why exactly do you have such a low opinion of them? they are all good people.</div> </div> </div> </div>They renamed the Uktena, Wendigo, and Fianna to be more sensitive. Changed totems to be more sensitive. They removed the Metis breed to be more sensitive. They removed kinfolk to avoid any appearance of eugenics to be more sensitive. All sensational things to get people talking. <br /> <br /> Here's an opportunity for them to show they were actually practicing what they preach and they failed utterly. They failed in not catching it. They failed in not admitting fault and apologizing when it was brought to their attention. They failed by giving their errand person platitudes and sending them back to the forums with &quot;they'll fix it they said so.&quot; <br /> <br /> Why am I hard on them? Because they put on airs that they were going to be better, then with the very first tribal preview they show it was all just publicity and they're not doing better at all. <br /> <br /> You claim they're good people but frankly, I sure don't see it. <br /> <br /> Now maybe they have already reached out to the victim (which seems the wrong word to use here but I can't think of anything else) and they're waiting to hear back from him. Hell, maybe he used to play W:tA with the artist and he was excited to have his likeness done for his favorite tribe. If so, then I'm wrong and I'll apologize, but I doubt that is the case, and it certainly isn't what they have claimed. <br /> <br /> I'd rather be wrong on the side I'm on than be wrong on the side of they'll fix it without prompting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T23:00:50-07:00","id":1510164,"title":"","content":"It goes right back to my &quot;stepping on toes&quot; analogy. They might not be maliciously bad people, but at a certain point, it's hard to treat them as good people if they keep making these mistakes and don't stop to figure out why and then make sure it stops happening.<br /> <br /> I don't think they're some sort of group of irredeemable horrors, but something is wrong in how Paradox is organizing the WoD teams. &quot;Good&quot; people need to fix this, not just keep apologizing for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T23:30:39-07:00","id":1510165,"title":"","content":"The tweet is still up - they have been told that artwork depicting T\u0101me Iti's likeness and tattoos without his permission is offensive to his culture, and the tweet with the image is still up. Deleting it and replacing with an apology tweet would be the first step.<br /> <br /> I'd never heard of T\u0101me before today, and I didn't know his culture's tattoos are sacred; I'm not from NZ, and honestly I think it's 100% possible a random artist, pressed for a deadline was told &quot;add a native face&quot; and just grabbed something off google. Failure on the artist's part, failure on the part of the art director, the sensitivity readers, and ultimately the buck stops with the people in charge for not having the right systems in place to prevent this. But. Mistakes do happen. They, like me, happened to not know this dude or his work, or his culture's beliefs about sacred body art. That's fine. What isn't fine is leaving the image up and giving a weak apology which doesn't even address the issue or apologize to the guy in question. A real apology explains what you did wrong, that you were wrong to do it, indicates you won't do it again, and THEN asks for forgiveness - often with an acknowledgement that forgiveness is optional, earned, not automatic.<br /> <br /> All of this is more galling given that the 'spin' on previous editions seems to have been &quot;the fans of old editions are racist grognards who loved Racism<b><sup>TM</sup></b>&quot;, meanwhile we are going to make a modern, inoffensive, baggage-free version of Werewolf for a new generation of unproblematic fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-30-2023, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T00:17:13-07:00","id":1510167,"title":"","content":"I see that as a bit more than a failure on the art director's fault (if it was what happened, we don't know). If the art director is supposed to make sure that W5 has a large amount of ethnic diversity represented to sell the Garou as a global phenomena (by itself a fine idea for the aims of the book), the art director should be getting the native/indigenous/other minority art assignments out ASAP because they're going to need the most sensitivity passes. If you need to put some art off for crunch reasons, it should be the stuff that will be perceived as more generic/less coded to a specific group.<br /> <br /> As well, one of the problems with getting freelance artists to do more diversity is that they default to the exact opposite. Freelance artists tend to treat art director prompts very literally, and don't &quot;go rogue&quot; because that's a good way to not get hired again. Justin Achilli himself has a great story about his experience as art director for the Rage CCG, where he asked for the Zmei card to be a dragon eating some clown in half. Having meant &quot;clown&quot; in a more figurative way, he ended up with an actual clown getting bit in half by a Zmei. It's ridiculous (but also kinda awesome if you Google the card and/or story), but it's predictable enough that most art directors learn to be very specific about these things. Exalted 3e's early art also had a problem where a few of the artists were not getting the message of how ethnically diverse Exalted is supposed to be, and a few pieces had to be recolored (perhaps multiple times) to get the range of skin tones desired.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to say anyone here did anything malicious, but that it's really hard to see this as a mistake that just couldn't have been avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T00:52:50-07:00","id":1510172,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the question is how deep the carelessness is running here. Starting with the artist just carelessly depicting indigenous people and then nobody properly supervising this and checking up on it could create a lot of issues at this stage. If nobody has ever bothered to look into what the art in the book is depicting then it's of course hard to detect mistakes. Like, if you carelessly just put a drawing of a Maori into your book and that's the beginning and end of anybody's research on that, of course, everybody will remain completely unaware of the particular cultural sensitivity surrounding their tattoos, for example. And so figuring out if there are more mistakes lurking in this book will be quite the task if the process that produced it was that careless and uncurious when it comes to what they are depicting in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T01:06:26-07:00","id":1510174,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder how much the diversity consultants are actually listened to and given chances to see the final product. Because what with this AND the H5 Jewish sledgehammer dude, I get the feeling the diversity consultants only see the text and not the art at all.<br /> <br /> That and maybe seek out artists of certain communities to do the art? I mean, what better way to show diversity than try to ensure your art team is varied?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T01:21:10-07:00","id":1510175,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that part of the problem is that they tend to have consultants (on some level, sometimes it's just a freelancer that's writing what they know like the Philippines part of H5) for areas of focus for the books. That's why this is so frequently smaller individual &quot;moments&quot; in the text rather than getting big sections off. So, they might have really invest in Native American/First People consultants because of WtA's history, but they might not know anything about Maori culture so they could miss it as easily as anyone else. If this is basically the only point in W5 were a Maori character comes up, so they didn't bother retaining a Maori sensitivity reader, it explains how they might listen to their consultants just fine, and still so many of these slip through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T02:19:44-07:00","id":1510179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510174#post1510174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder how much the diversity consultants are actually listened to and given chances to see the final product. Because what with this AND the H5 Jewish sledgehammer dude, I get the feeling the diversity consultants only see the text and not the art at all.<br /> <br /> That and maybe seek out artists of certain communities to do the art? I mean, what better way to show diversity than try to ensure your art team is varied?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you got a link to this Hunter thing I keep hearing about, with the hammer? Just wanna see how blatant it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T03:17:54-07:00","id":1510181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510179#post1510179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you got a link to this Hunter thing I keep hearing about, with the hammer? Just wanna see how blatant it is.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/HOkgA46.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.imgur.com/HOkgA46.jpg</a> the art.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483651#post1483651\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...51#post1483651</a> Hevy Arm's analysis of the art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T03:31:59-07:00","id":1510183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510181#post1510181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/HOkgA46.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.imgur.com/HOkgA46.jpg</a> the art.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483651#post1483651\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...51#post1483651</a> Hevy Arm's analysis of the art.</div> </div> </div> </div>So immediately the image makes me laugh - the musculature isn't absurd but the overall IMAGE is absurd. The analysis is helpful because it helps pin down a lot of things which just feel vaguely wrong at a glance and verbalize why it's so weird. Overall I'm happier with the image than I was expecting, because based on &quot;bad image of a Jewish hunter in H5&quot; my initial expectation was a directly anti-semitic caricature. Instead... very poorly researched yet trying-to-be-positive caricature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T04:41:50-07:00","id":1510190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510183#post1510183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So immediately the image makes me laugh - the musculature isn't absurd but the overall IMAGE is absurd. The analysis is helpful because it helps pin down a lot of things which just feel vaguely wrong at a glance and verbalize why it's so weird. Overall I'm happier with the image than I was expecting, because based on &quot;bad image of a Jewish hunter in H5&quot; my initial expectation was a directly anti-semitic caricature. Instead... very poorly researched yet trying-to-be-positive caricature?</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly found the image uninteresting without the explanation. With it the character suddenly has a really interesting story and I'm furious it was almost certainly unintentional.<br /> <br /> Like, I want this guy to be an iconic character who reappears in the books, has an arc, and has his background fleshed out so people like me understand all these cues in his outfit. Not to play him, I'd much rather be a MMA-practicing nun, but have him be more than a token image to inspire people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T06:40:00-07:00","id":1510195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510190#post1510190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly found the image uninteresting without the explanation. With it the character suddenly has a really interesting story and I'm furious it was almost certainly unintentional.<br /> <br /> Like, I want this guy to be an iconic character who reappears in the books, has an arc, and has his background fleshed out so people like me understand all these cues in his outfit. Not to play him, I'd much rather be a MMA-practicing nun, but have him be more than a token image to inspire people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. That's a damn good explanarion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T11:09:31-07:00","id":1510219,"title":"","content":"I think they've done an exceptionally good job at being bland, boring, unfun and uninspired. It's as if someone was being paid for word count and had no actual passion for the project. Werewolf was always meant to be extreme, and Glass walkers were no exception to that. Where's my Wise Guy, my digital wolf, my green haired transhuman cyborg, my power-armoured furry rocking 20mm? None of that. We have a city planner who wants to ease traffic jams and add a few green spaces rather than pedestrianize the whole city. Why so moderate. It's very evident they don't care. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bit puzzled as to how a Maori would end up a poster boy for a werewolf tribe when NZ has never had wolves, and why he'd have a vastly different tattoo style on his arm... Like, even if we ignore the copying bit, that's stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T11:16:10-07:00","id":1510223,"title":"","content":"That last part may be in part due to the bits of Forsaken DNA that got splashed in, as I'm fairly certain that there can be Forsaken and Pure fighting over places where wolves never were, as the presence or absence of wolves never played a factor in their existence. It's also probably part of the &quot;Garou don't know how Garou come about&quot; bits of this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T11:20:00-07:00","id":1510224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510219#post1510219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they've done an exceptionally good job at being bland, boring, unfun and uninspired. It's as if someone was being paid for word count and had no actual passion for the project. Werewolf was always meant to be extreme, and Glass walkers were no exception to that. Where's my Wise Guy, my digital wolf, my green haired transhuman cyborg, my power-armoured furry rocking 20mm? None of that. We have a city planner who wants to ease traffic jams and add a few green spaces rather than pedestrianize the whole city. Why so moderate. It's very evident they don't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've talked in this forum about the previews since last October and what you're describing here was the design-goal, I would say. W5 removed the ties to any human ethnicity and/or culture, most of the past lore was removed (if it isn't an event or lore-tidbit being mentioned it hasn't happened in this version) and instead of course W5-Tribes focus on the infamous <i>verbs</i>.<br /> <br /> Ultimately Tribe is a vehicle for &quot;what you do?&quot;. And... so that's how it's been written.<br /> <br /> Additionally, what I feel like both the introduction and the Glass-Walker-write-up have focused on is the idea that there are huge disagreements between the Garou-Tribes about what to do. Like every Tribe has its own kind of tunnel-vision when it comes to saving the world. (To me, this presentation just makes me wonder how there was ever a Garou-Nation in the first place but I guess we'll see how the book as a whole handles that.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T11:48:47-07:00","id":1510231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510223#post1510223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That last part may be in part due to the bits of Forsaken DNA that got splashed in, as I'm fairly certain that there can be Forsaken and Pure fighting over places where wolves never were, as the presence or absence of wolves never played a factor in their existence. It's also probably part of the &quot;Garou don't know how Garou come about&quot; bits of this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll have to see a bit on whether or not they actually bring in some of the key Forsaken elements that actually make this work. For example, since Forsaken werewolves are always born humans, they take on the physical characteristics of the dominant wild canids of an area rather than Apocalyse's explicit <i>Canis lupus</i> (without Mokole magic) only approach. Uratha born in Central and South America tend to look like maned wolves (which are technically foxes) because spirit logic isn't biology based, but rather filling the role of canid-hunter. They don't need the handwaving Apocalypse used to justify African hunting dogs, Indonesia singing dogs, or dingoes to be valid wolf-form-shapes for characters from those parts of the world.<br /> <br /> W5 might bring that over, making it a bit easier to globalize the Garou, but we'll have to see (esp. since it screws with some of the Fera).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T12:33:30-07:00","id":1510234,"title":"","content":"As if the Fera aren't getting reset anyway. If the ravenshifters in the corebook are the Corax I shall purchases a trilby and two slices of bread.<br /> <br /> With any luck the Nuwisha, Kitsune, and any other canid shifters I've forgotten will get quietly folded into the Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 04-30-2023, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T12:48:08-07:00","id":1510236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510219#post1510219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they've done an exceptionally good job at being bland, boring, unfun and uninspired. It's as if someone was being paid for word count and had no actual passion for the project. Werewolf was always meant to be extreme, and Glass walkers were no exception to that. Where's my Wise Guy, my digital wolf, my green haired transhuman cyborg, my power-armoured furry rocking 20mm? None of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there is no werewolf in the text. Not only that, but consider the given jobs as concepts. They are just... jobs. Even Forsaken, which by design is more grounded in everyday life, did not define their example characters by their jobs alone. Iron Masters might wear the sheepskin, but their actual concepts are the way their city skills benefit the pack, their concepts are the things they do as werewolves. The wolves who do wear a full on facade are members of a lodge dedicated for that purpose to get close to targets.<br /> <br /> These Walkers play by the book and the only one who doesn't is noted to be making excuses for themselves for what they do. Nothing in this preview reads like a creature of rage and anger at the world dying. Where is the horror?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T13:01:29-07:00","id":1510240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510223#post1510223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That last part may be in part due to the bits of Forsaken DNA that got splashed in, as I'm fairly certain that there can be Forsaken and Pure fighting over places where wolves never were, as the presence or absence of wolves never played a factor in their existence. It's also probably part of the &quot;Garou don't know how Garou come about&quot; bits of this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that definitely is part of W5 (at least according to the previews)! From the Discord Q&amp;A:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Does W5 still follow the assumption that werewolves only operate in countries where wolves exist in large numbers (that is, the northern hemisphere)?</b><br /> No, W5 assumes that most Garou are human, and that anywhere humans are, werewolves can exist. In places with different indigenous species, for example, I'd like to have some supplementary material in place, but W5 core is focused on werewolves. </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere's also a comment on what Garou look in wolf-form from JA:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Will there be a visual identity to the wolf form of each tribe like in previous editions, for instance silver fur for Silver Fangs or black and white fur for Black Furies?</b><br /> Not inherently, but you could certainly have them occur as part of the pact with the Patron Spirit. Definitely good for telegraphing clues to the players! </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T13:09:07-07:00","id":1510242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509727-glass-walkers-have-won-the-poll-for-a-preview?p=1510236#post1510236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, there is no werewolf in the text. Not only that, but consider the given jobs as concepts. They are just... jobs. Even Forsaken, which by design is more grounded in everyday life, did not define their example characters by their jobs alone. Iron Masters might wear the sheepskin, but their actual concepts are the way their city skills benefit the pack, their concepts are the things they do as werewolves. The wolves who do wear a full on facade are members of a lodge dedicated for that purpose to get close to targets.<br /> <br /> These Walkers play by the book and the only one who doesn't is noted to be making excuses for themselves for what they do. Nothing in this preview reads like a creature of rage and anger at the world dying. <b>Where is the horror?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, in making Garou tear their clothes when they shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"tha